    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "#  Overview\nAn automated B2B lead management workflow built with n8n and HubSpot. It captures leads through an n8n form, standardizes and stores their information in HubSpot, prevents duplicate contacts, calculates a lead score based on budget, company size, and required service, assigns a priority level, updates the CRM, and sends targeted email notifications to the lead and internal Slack alerts to the team.\n\n## Purpose & Key Objectives\nThe purpose of this workflow is to automate the journey from lead capture to CRM qualification and team notification, reducing manual data entry and ensuring every lead is consistently processed, scored, prioritized, and followed up with an appropriate response.\n",
        "height": 456,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "55701a82-4fdd-4beb-94ad-204e0c41b0b2",
      "name": "Note: Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -704,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Lead-to-CRM Qualification & Outreach Automation",
        "height": 80,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "da63d33d-ef94-4da6-aa9f-fd7237232c07",
      "name": "Note: Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        816,
        -144
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Node-by-Node Purpose\n\n1) **On Form Submission:**  \nTriggers automatically when a new lead submits the n8n form and starts the lead-processing workflow.\n\n2) **Normalize Lead Data:**  \nCleans and standardizes the submitted lead information into a consistent format for CRM processing.\n\n3) **HubSpot – Search Contact:**  \nChecks HubSpot using the lead’s email address to identify whether an existing contact already exists.\n\n4) **HubSpot – Create or Update Existing Contact:**  \nCreates a new HubSpot contact when none exists, or updates the existing contact with the latest submitted information.\n\n5) **Prepare Lead Data:**  \nExtracts the required CRM fields such as name, email, company, service, company size, and budget into a clean structure.\n\n6) **Calculate Lead Score:**  \nCalculates a qualification score using budget, company size, and requested service to measure lead quality.\n\n7) **Route Lead by Score:**  \nRoutes the lead into High, Medium, or Low priority based on the calculated lead score.\n\n8) **Set Lead Priority:**  \nAssigns the corresponding priority level (High, Medium, or Low) to the lead while preserving the rest of the lead data.\n\n9) **Merge Leads:**  \nCombines the priority branches back into a single workflow path.\n\n10) **Update Lead Qualification:**  \nSaves the calculated lead_score and lead_priority back to the HubSpot contact.\n\n11) **Route Follow-Up:**  \nRoutes the qualified lead to the appropriate communication path based on its priority.\n\n12) **High-Priority Email + Slack:**  \nSends a direct client email and alerts the internal team in Slack to prioritize immediate follow-up.\n\n13) **Medium-Priority Email + Slack:**  \nSends a professional follow-up email and notifies the team that the lead requires normal sales follow-up.\n\n14) **Low-Priority Email + Slack:**  \nSends a low-pressure client acknowledgement and alerts the team to place the lead into the nurture/follow-up queue.",
        "height": 1220,
        "width": 552,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "32a5bbda-3de9-4789-a166-238bd6a72012",
      "name": "Note: Node-by-node",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2288,
        -304
      ]
    }
  ],
